       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4000 mg four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day, which is 5 times the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen. The usual ceiling is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use, given as up to 800 mg per dose. A dose that high risks serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular and CNS toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo, for example 400 mg instead of 4000 mg. Which of these did you mean?\n\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a common analgesic or anti-inflammatory dose\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Another regimen\n\nIf 4000 mg per dose is what you intended, tell me and I'll review it with you before entering anything."
